{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require a General Election if the Prime Minister changes mid-term in Parliament",
        "additional_details": "Under the current UK political system, Prime Minister can be replaced in the middle of the parliamentary term before the next General Election by internal party processes. \r\n \r\nWhile voters elect local MPs, the party leader heavily influences the public's choice based on their specific commitments. We believe replacing a Prime Minister mid-term without consulting the public undermines the democratic mandate. Parliament should legislate so that a change of party leadership mid-term triggers a general election, unless the incumbent steps down due to severe, verified ill health.",
        "background": "We call on Parliament to legislate to require an automatic General Election if there is a change of leadership during the parliamentary term from any political party that was voted into power at the General Election, with exemptions for severe, verified cases of ill health.",
